@1101 = ~Incarnation of the Spirit of the Great Worm~
@1102 = ~Rid me of this parasite...~
@1103 = ~Adventurers? Here? Finally! If you figured out how to get here, then you know how to get out. Tell me!~
@1104 = ~I have to destroy the boss of this area to obtain a rune, and then use that rune.~
@1105 = ~If you're the boss, you should know that.~
@1106 = ~A spirit asked me to rid it of you. Prepare to die.~
@1107 = ~I don't have a rune. I don't know what rune you're talking about... You're lying! Fine. I'll find whatever I need on your corpse.~
@1108 = ~You're telling me that I should know? I've been holed up in this tiny place for more than 20 years, doing nothing but fending off every attempt by those filthy lizards to get in, without ever seeing any possible way out, and you're telling me I should know? Unless... You're accusing me of lying, is that it? The thief accused me of lying too... he got what he deserved. And so will you.~
@1109 = ~A spirit? There is no spirit up there, only those damned lizards. I know! You're trying to confuse me. The paladin tried to confuse me too. He died for it. And so will you.~
@11010 = ~Piece of leather~
@11011 = ~On this large piece of leather of dubious origin, someone has written what looks like a journal: "I'm going mad. They're all dead. Dead. I'm the only one still alive. I was the cleverest. Now I'm nothing, and I'm going mad. I hear them walking overhead. They scratch at the barrier, they want to get in. But they won't get in. The barrier is too powerful for their filthy mugs. They breathe fire, they want to burn it; but they won't manage it, I made it indestructible. I won't die. I've survived this far, and I'll survive longer. Without my food-creation spells, I would have died long ago; but always the same spell... always the same food. Eventually I couldn't stand it anymore. I'm going mad. And this place, ridiculously small, does it even exist, or am I imagining it? My prayers go unanswered. The spells come to me as they do every morning, but I haven't heard Rao's voice since that accursed day when we entered this infernal gauntlet. There were eight of us. Or seven, I don't know anymore. We were powerful, and sure of ourselves... nonsense. No one is ever powerful enough. The elf fell first when the chasm swallowed her. The paladin's grief proved fatal. The mage was prepared for anything, but not the thief's betrayal. The barbarian should not have gotten involved... the thief had thought of everything. Except losing his head to the dwarf's axe. There were only three of us left when we saw the dragons. They ate the dwarf and the warrior. I rushed into this hole, and I curse them all for leaving me alone. Shalierra... Why did you leave me? Why did you let Blackhand attack you? Didn't you see it coming? Really? Or did you do it on purpose? This gauntlet is driving us all mad, but I'd been crazy about you from the moment I met you. Oh... Shalierra... can you see me from where you are?
Ah, they're scratching again. Let them come. I've set traps. Dragons or not, they won't withstand a Finger of Death improved by years of preparation. Let them come, and perhaps this nightmare will finally end. Shalierra, I'm coming....".~
@11012 = ~Dragonborn Smasher~
@11013 = ~Green Half-Dragon~
@11014 = ~Red Half-Dragon~
@11015 = ~Green Dragon~
@11016 = ~I can feel that the parasite is gone. Thank you, adventurer. Receive my blessing. And take that stone from the sand behind my messenger.~~I can feel that the parasite is gone. Thank you, adventurer. Receive my blessing. And take that stone from the sand behind my messenger.~
@11017 = ~"Nerull, I implore you. Have you forgotten me? Will you let yokels destroy your devoted servant?"~
@11018 = ~The dwarf~ //n
@11019 = ~The elf~ //e
@11020 = ~The barbarian~ //b
@11021 = ~The paladin~ //p
@11022 = ~The warrior~ //g
@11023 = ~The thief~ //v
@11024 = ~The mage~ //m
@11025 = ~Use an item~
@11026 = ~An invisible barrier prevents you from passing. You can sense that something divine is behind it.~
@11027 = ~Wait, wasn't that one blue?~
@11028 = ~The elf's animal companion~
@11029 = ~Watch closely, elf. I'll show you what a ranged weapon is.~ //nain
@11030 = ~Let's fight!~ //barbare
@11031 = ~As always, dwarf, you're talking nonsense.~ //elfe
@11032 = ~Comrades, such childishness is beneath you.~ //paladin
@11033 = ~I see you've finally understood...~ //voleur
@11034 = ~Heey, hi Tibalun :)~ //guerrier
@11035 = ~Nothing is insurmountable when you're prepared.~ //Mage
@11036 = ~Avatar of Nerull~
@11037 = ~Mortals, you who destroy my immortal servants: the Reaper has come for you.~
@11038 = ~*notices the priest*: Tibalun, I can see it: you've turned to the dark side.~ //paladin 2
@11039 = ~Sand Tornado~
@11040 = ~Come on, everyone, let's do this together!~

@11050 = ~Holy Symbol of Rao~
@11051 = ~This is the stone symbol of a god you do not know. It inspires serenity.

STATISTICS

Equipped abilities:
Memorization: +1 spell slot at 6th and 7th level.
Magic Resistance: +5%.
Strength: +1.~

@11052 = ~Holy Symbol of Nerull~
@11053 = ~This is the wooden symbol of a god you do not know. It bodes ill.

STATISTICS

Equipped abilities:
Memorization: +1 spell slot at 6th and 7th level.
Magic Resistance: +5%.
Strength: +1.~

